{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarParityZeta4Swap","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CuspShapeBarParity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity.cusp_barParity_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity.cusp_barParity_split","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L82-L89","doc":"**Cusp bar-parity split (paper statement).** The figure-eight cusp shape\n`ω` (root of `Φ₆`) splits under the bar involution into a rational Volume part\n`barEven ω = 1` and a `√−3` Chern–Simons part `barOdd ω ^ 2 = −3` — the\n`𝔙 = Vol + i·CS` grading of the complex volume, realised algebraically. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:cusp-shape-bar-parity","label":"prop:cusp-shape-bar-parity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/cusp-shape-bar-parity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity.holonomy_hyperbola","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity.holonomy_hyperbola","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/CuspShapeBarParity.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**Boost hyperbola.** The meridian holonomy `q` (any nonzero field element)\nsatisfies `barEven q ² − barOdd q ² = 4` — the `cosh² − sinh² = 1` identity.\nOne meridian turn is a hyperbolic rotation.\n\n§7c note: the difference is `4·q·q⁻¹`, so the proof is a single explicit\nunit witness (`q · q⁻¹ = 1`) rather than a `field_simp` denominator clear.\nThe `[Field R]` on the section variable is *not* removable here — it is\ninherited from `barEven` / `barOdd`, which are defined with the ring\ninverse `x⁻¹` in `QOU.QBeta.BarParityZeta4Swap`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meridian-holonomy-boost","label":"prop:meridian-holonomy-boost","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meridian-holonomy-boost.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}